  "sourceCommit": "1430890a33e360e272da74943b17415d70575ef3",
  "nextAction": "D252 / S03.acceptance: implement the verified grant client 429 protocol gap after bounded review of current WebLicense client/cache/controller contracts. The server now returns grant-only 429 with Retry-After, but the current client discards it as network-unavailable and permits another immediate online check. Add an explicit identity/context-scoped cooldown derived only from the valid server header, preserving abort/generation fencing and clock/expiry rules; do not invent a provider threshold or grant permission from 429. Before the deadline repeated online checks must not fetch; at the deadline a fresh check may resume. Malformed headers must not create a permanent lock. Preserve valid independently verified offline proof, subject/key/signature binding and exclusive offlineUntil/expiry; 429 is not revocation and must not erase it. Add meaningful focused tests for cooldown/no-fetch, deadline recovery, malformed-header handling, context isolation and superseded/aborted replies. Keep scope on grant/session client behavior; no new account/bootstrap UX, server policy changes, SDK/provider activation, database apply, deploy or unrelated app/PWA/native builds. Preserve D251 evidence from 165/165 tests tied to source and unchanged S03/COMMERCE acceptance statuses; no live-provider, concurrency or release claim.",
